{
  "_comment": [
    "Copy this file to .clasp.json and fill in your own scriptId.",
    "The real .clasp.json is gitignored because the script ID is specific to",
    "your Google account.",
    "",
    "Find your scriptId in the Apps Script editor under Project Settings (gear",
    "icon) -> IDs -> Script ID.",
    "",
    "  npm install -g @google/clasp",
    "  clasp login",
    "  clasp pull      downloads what is live, into src/",
    "  clasp push      uploads src/ to the project",
    "",
    "fileExtension MATTERS, AND LEAVING IT OUT IS A TRAP.",
    "",
    "clasp names server files .js by default. This repository names them .gs.",
    "Pull without this line and you do not get your files updated - you get a",
    "SECOND copy of every one of them: Config.gs from git sitting beside a",
    "Config.js that clasp just wrote. Nothing looks wrong, because the .js",
    "files are untracked and git says little about them.",
    "",
    "The next push is where it goes wrong. clasp treats .gs and .js alike, so",
    "it uploads both, and the Apps Script project ends up with every function",
    "declared twice. That is not a subtle fault - the project stops running.",
    "",
    "So: keep the line. If a pull ever writes .js files into src/, stop before",
    "pushing anything and delete them.",
    "",
    "AND PUSHING IS NOT DEPLOYING. clasp push changes the code; the live URL",
    "goes on serving the old version until somebody does Deploy -> Manage",
    "deployments -> pencil -> Version: New version -> Deploy.",
    "",
    "Pasting into the editor works perfectly well too. clasp is a convenience,",
    "not a requirement."
  ],
  "scriptId": "PASTE_YOUR_SCRIPT_ID_HERE",
  "rootDir": "src",
  "fileExtension": "gs"
}
